ledge retrieval#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[35,36],"#Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[37,39],"#Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[38,39],"#Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[40,42],"#Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[41,42],"#Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[43,44]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/39JP5FYC","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/5MMDHYPG?page=1&annotation=FV4PYSPB","line":35},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/5MMDHYPG?page=10&annotation=7PG9WDTK","line":35},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/5MMDHYPG?page=1&annotation=XA4KF2D8","line":38},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/5MMDHYPG?page=1&annotation=8N6UHE52","line":41}],"metadata":{"Title":"Evaluation of LLMs accuracy and consistency in the registered dietitian exam through prompt engineering and knowledge retrieval","Authors":"Iman Azimi, Mohan Qi, Li Wang, Amir M. Rahmani, Youlin Li","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1038/s41598-024-85003-w","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"In this paper, we propose to employ the Registered Dietitian (RD) exam to conduct a standard and comprehensive evaluation of state-of-the-art LLMs, GPT-4o, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, and Gemini 1.5 Pro, assessing both accuracy and consistency in nutrition queries.techniques: 1) Zero Shot prompting (ZS), 2) Chain of Thought (CoT), 3) Chain of Thought with Self Consistency (CoT-SC), and 4) Retrieval Augmented Prompting (RAP) enabled by external nutrition knowledge.","Findings":"Our findings revealed that while these LLMs obtained acceptable overall performance, their results varied considerably with different prompts and question domains.  GPT-4o with CoT-SC prompting outperformed the other approaches, whereas Gemini 1.5 Pro with ZS recorded the highest consistenc","Conclusions":"Consequently, choosing the appropriate LLM and prompting technique, tailored to the proficiency level and specific domain, can mitigate errors and potential risks in diet and nutrition chatbots.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"prompt görmedim ama gerekli.  dyt karşılaştırmasından emin olamadım."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1botouy","at":1774939764524},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/azimiEvaluationLLMsAccuracy2025b.md"},
